        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 3:24PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 324 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Rio En Medio in Santa Fe County, or 10 miles north of Santa Fe,
moving north at 35 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Chimayo, Pojoaque, Cundiyo, Rio Chiquito, Nambe Pueblo, Truchas, La
Puebla, Nambe Lake and Cuartelez.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.

Motorists can expect brief but sudden changes in visibility and
ponding of water on roadways as storms move through the area.</instruction>
